From b00f235aa079cd62f4405c2818dca38406ab1ca2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:03:24 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Network page: no ImGui ID warning for players, who is online,
 typed servers remembered

- ImGui's "conflicting ID" box is a message for developers; it showed
  to a player on the Steam Deck. <PREFIX>_UI_ID_CHECK=1 now turns it on,
  and it is off otherwise. The status rows whose labels can repeat (hosts
  heard, peers, sockets) get an ID each.
- Hosting counts the players online ("2 players online"): a player who
  joins on this page appears once their game goes online. A joining
  player gets a row "Joined <address>   connects when you go online".
- A server typed into the Server field is remembered under Join, as one
  typed under Address is (adhoc_remember()).
- <PREFIX>_EXAMPLE_ADDRESSES=1 also shows sessions heard on the network
  under documentation addresses (192.0.2.100 on), for pictures of the page.
- "Online" and "offline" as one word throughout the Network page, its
  help and the ad hoc code's comments.

Tested with Dissidia 012 on Windows and a Steam Deck: two copies on one
PC into a battle, each stepping through the whole Network page with
<PREFIX>_UI_ID_CHECK=1, no warning; a Windows setup install against the
Deck over a LAN and over a mobile hotspot, battles in step to their end,
the Deck remembering the LAN and the internet address. Not seen: the
duplicate rows the Deck had before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
